# MOVEMENT PATTERNS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Movement Patterns define the fundamental language of human movement inside the Combat Athlete System.

Exercises are implementations.

Movement patterns are the underlying concepts.

CAS reasons using movement patterns before selecting exercises.

---

# Philosophy

An athlete does not need a Back Squat.

An athlete needs the adaptations produced by the Squat pattern.

Different exercises may satisfy the same movement requirement.

Movement patterns therefore remain stable,

while exercise selection may change.

---

# Scientific Role

Movement patterns connect:

Biomechanics

↓

Physical Capabilities

↓

Exercise Selection

↓

Sport Transfer

↓

Session Generation

Every engine should reason through movement patterns.

---

# Design Principles

Movement patterns must be:

Universal

Scientifically meaningful

Independent of equipment

Independent of exercise popularity

Applicable across all combat sports

Stable over time

---

